cing services. In addition, the company offers payment solutions, such as acceptance, processing, and settlement of credit card and debit card payments, financial processing services for freestanding ATMs; digital payments; and merchant services, as well as issues debit and prepaid cards. The company was formerly known as Meta Financial Group, Inc. and changed its name to Pathward Financial, Inc. in July 2022. Pathward Financial, Inc. was founded in 1954 and is based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brett L. Pharr | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $686K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $359K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Pathward Financial, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.4B market cap on $840M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +22% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 25% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 15-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $439M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 52 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.42\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 19\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder 